    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete. Let me summarize what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and moved every value derived from it onto the new identity. The build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0`), and the audit log now shows codes like `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`IdentityKeyResolver.java`** \u2014 added `deriveCustomerCode(Owner)`, the single home for the new identity:\n- `REGION` = region code from the postcode (`Region.forPostcode`), falling back to `UNKNOWN` when the postcode maps to no known region.\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`, where `normalizedTelephone` uses the existing `TelephoneNormalizer.canonicalize`.\n- Extracted the SHA-256 hex logic into a shared `upperHexDigest(value, chars)` helper, which `deriveHouseholdId` now also uses (its output is unchanged).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `addOwner` now calls `identityKeyResolver.deriveCustomerCode(owner)`, and the old per-city sequence generator `generateCustomerCode` was deleted. The membership number, its check digit, and the create audit record all read from `customerCode`, so they follow the new identity automatically.\n\n**`LocalityResolver.java` + `OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 locality derivation moved onto the new identity: `deriveLocality` now takes the `customerCode` and returns its `REGION` segment (`UNKNOWN` when absent), instead of recomputing from city/postcode. The mapper wiring was updated accordingly.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber` example, and `locality` descriptions to document the new region-and-hash identity.\n\n### Behaviour notes\n- Sequence numbers are gone entirely; the code is now a pure function of postcode, telephone, and last name.\n- This is a deliberate behaviour change (per the spec): locality no longer falls back to the city-to-region table \u2014 it reflects the postcode-derived region carried in the `customerCode`. Seed owners (no `customerCode`) resolve to `UNKNOWN`, matching their prior result.",
